WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.245
Lesson 6.1.

00:00:02.245 --> 00:00:04.000
Protocol due diligence.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.021
By the end of this lesson, you'll be

00:00:06.021 --> 00:00:08.205
able to run the 6-step research loop on

00:00:08.205 --> 00:00:10.335
a protocol and reach a written verdict.

00:00:11.635 --> 00:00:12.925
Here's the plan.

00:00:12.925 --> 00:00:14.610
First, the key ideas.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:17.325
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:17.325 --> 00:00:18.850
Then, your checklist.

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:21.012
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:22.312 --> 00:00:25.076
Log it in the DeFi Protocol Due Diligence

00:00:25.076 --> 00:00:27.839
Tracker (Notion) and tick a box only when

00:00:27.839 --> 00:00:30.442
the step is evidenced, not assumed.

00:00:30.442 --> 00:00:35.285
First, Mechanism: what the contracts do; users, assets, incentives.

00:00:35.285 --> 00:00:39.425
Next, Cash flow: real fees and interest vs emissions.

00:00:39.425 --> 00:00:45.525
Then, Dependencies: oracles, bridges, admin keys, stablecoins, other protocols.

00:00:45.525 --> 00:00:50.769
Also, Solvency: collateral quality, liquidation design, bad-debt paths.

00:00:50.769 --> 00:00:52.461
On top of that, Evidence:

00:00:52.461 --> 00:00:55.584
explorers, audits, governance, independent data.

00:00:56.885 --> 00:00:59.365
And finally, Exit: exact unwind,

00:00:59.365 --> 00:01:01.995
gas, slippage, approvals to revoke.

00:01:03.295 --> 00:01:05.810
Let's work an example, step by step.

00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:08.425
"Protocol Y (lending, Arbitrum).

00:01:08.425 --> 00:01:09.860
Risk: Medium.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:13.276
Fees are real (borrow demand $2M/yr), but

00:01:13.276 --> 00:01:16.936
one collateral uses a thin-market oracle and

00:01:16.936 --> 00:01:19.595
upgrades have a 24h timelock.

00:01:19.595 --> 00:01:22.975
Verdict: supply stablecoins only, cap at 10% of

00:01:22.975 --> 00:01:25.862
the DeFi book, alert on queued upgrades."

00:01:27.162 --> 00:01:28.622
Here's your checklist.

00:01:28.622 --> 00:01:30.157
Do it now, for real.

00:01:30.157 --> 00:01:32.772
First, all six steps written with sources.

00:01:32.772 --> 00:01:34.634
Next, Risk rating = worst

00:01:34.634 --> 00:01:37.082
material risk, not an average.

00:01:37.082 --> 00:01:40.517
And finally, Verdict states size, conditions and exit.

00:01:41.817 --> 00:01:43.027
Question 1.

00:01:43.027 --> 00:01:44.217
Why is the rating the

00:01:44.217 --> 00:01:45.732
worst risk, not the average?

00:01:50.152 --> 00:01:52.105
The answer: One failure point is

00:01:52.105 --> 00:01:53.762
enough to lose the position.

00:01:55.062 --> 00:01:56.307
Question 2.

00:01:56.307 --> 00:01:57.962
Which step prevents getting stuck?

00:02:02.382 --> 00:02:04.457
The answer: Step 6: Exit.

00:02:05.757 --> 00:02:07.027
Question 3.

00:02:07.027 --> 00:02:08.592
When do you tick a tracker box?

00:02:13.012 --> 00:02:15.467
The answer: Only when there's evidence for it.

00:02:16.767 --> 00:02:18.012
Let's recap.

00:02:18.012 --> 00:02:20.317
Mechanism: what the contracts do.

00:02:20.317 --> 00:02:23.881
Cash flow: real fees and interest vs emissions.

00:02:23.881 --> 00:02:29.429
Dependencies: oracles, bridges, admin keys, stablecoins, other protocols.

00:02:29.429 --> 00:02:33.840
Solvency: collateral quality, liquidation design, bad-debt paths.

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:37.655
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:02:37.655 --> 00:02:40.599
Next up, Lesson 6.2: Tokenomics:

00:02:40.599 --> 00:02:43.810
supply, unlocks, FDV, value capture.
